<p>President Trump has asked Congress to approve a roughly $1.5 trillion US defense budget for fiscal year 2027, a proposal that would sharply increase military spending while cutting non-defense discretionary programs by 10%. Multiple reports say the request reflects the administration’s priorities as the United States faces rising costs from its war with Iran, broader security commitments, and the need to rebuild weapons stockpiles. The blueprint would push defense spending to about 4.5% of US gross domestic product, according to NDTV, and several outlets describe it as a roughly 40%-44% increase from current levels, with about $500 billion in additional military funding. The plan is likely to face close scrutiny in Congress because it pairs military expansion with cuts to domestic programs, underscoring a clear choice about how Washington should allocate resources during an active overseas conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/6T_NPKV8c_XFqG0bC9h51ipTXVNBw4hJwUhTxtA7i3tX-8Xoylsz-O2vyeMZl2TjEFYJDuF-PbvBKxlM2N2q23FHzAQPTYdQlqtN8G7djHPBXMC1tkSlrrIBi4hQgoIkL69Y1Q787T3UmMhQPvfcc_f4EkSHFrrXFay3gtQy0edncY9yW6oDBhbTxo0DR00sTMhvZywieo8HtdHNiaQv5U6NqdbQ7PTVdEWy4BlI_bEuJa8PEIye5RkGhw' alt='The Pentagon and the surrounding area is seen in this aerial view in Washington, January 26, 2020.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Golden Dome: NDTV reports that the proposal includes funding for a &quot;Golden Dome&quot; missile-defense push, highlighting the administration’s interest in expanding homeland protection systems alongside broader military spending.</li><li>Stockpile rebuild: The White House says part of the increase is needed to replenish weapons inventories, a pressure point that has grown with the Iran war and wider US security commitments.</li><li>Domestic cuts: President Trump said he wants to reduce or eliminate what he called &quot;woke, weaponized and wasteful programs,&quot; framing the planned 10% reduction in non-defense discretionary spending in political terms.</li><li>Congressional test: The request is a budget blueprint, not enacted law, so lawmakers will still have to negotiate funding levels and could reshape both defense and domestic spending before final approval.</li></ul><blockquote>It’s not possible for us to take care of day care, Medicaid, Medicare, all of these individual things, they can do it on a state basis. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: The administration presented the request as a response to wartime costs, global security obligations, and the need to rebuild military stockpiles, making defense its clearest budget priority. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-1-5t-for-defense-10-cut-to-domestic-programs/a-76657289'>DW</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump argued that federal priorities should favor military protection over programs such as child care and suggested that states should take on more responsibility for social spending. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/02/us/politics/trump-military-spending-budget.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>BBC analysis: BBC reporting emphasized that the blueprint ties a large defense increase to broad domestic cuts, setting up a fight in Congress over competing national priorities. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crr1q4kjvn2o'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>World Socialist Web Site: WSWS described the plan as a historic military escalation paired with deep social cuts, interpreting the proposal as financing war through domestic austerity. (<a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/04/04/ahuk-a04.html'>World Socialist Web Site</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/donald-trump-defense-proposal-middle-east-war-inside-1-5-trillion-ask-11309526#publisher=newsstand'>Golden Dome, War Funds And Cuts: Inside Trump&#x27;s Defence Proposal</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-1-5t-for-defense-10-cut-to-domestic-programs/a-76657289'>Trump seeks $1.5T for defense, 10% cut to domestic programs</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/04/04/ahuk-a04.html'>Trump’s plan to fund world war through social counter-revolution</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/white-house-budget-defence-trump-iran-war/article70820129.ece'>White House seeks $1.5 trillion defence budget as Iran war drives costs</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/03/white-house-asks-for-massive-1-5-trillion-defense-budget-a-40-increase_6752097_4.html'>White House asks for massive $1.5 trillion defense budget – a 40% increase</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/03/2026/white-house-asks-congress-to-spend-big-on-defense'>White House asks Congress to spend big on defense</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1sbnrr5/trump_requests_recordbreaking_budget_of_15/'>Trump requests record-breaking budget of $1.5 trillion for Pentagon</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crr1q4kjvn2o'>Trump seeks $1.5tn for defence alongside domestic spending cuts</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/news-wrap-trump-seeking-1-5-trillion-for-military-spending-in-new-budget'>News Wrap: Trump seeking $1.5 trillion for military spending in new budget</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/politics/article/3349007/trump-administration-seeks-us15-trillion-defence-new-budget-request'>Trump seeks US$1.5 trillion for defence in new budget request amid Iran war</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/02/us/politics/trump-military-spending-budget.html'>War With Iran Clarifies Trump’s Spending Priorities: The Military, Not Child Care</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>